 or DELETE with `mcp-session-id: constructor` or `__proto__`","reason":"DELETE is assessed in the same finding for lookup and error handling, and it has its own test case. Finding 2 also notes that DELETE only delegates to handleRequest. The two handlers are identical, so the report treats them together."},{"id":"coverage_launch","met":true,"report_quote":"HTTP wrapper `register(app, createTransport)` in `repo/service/routes.mjs`, entrypoint per `repo/launch.json`.","reason":"The report resolves the entrypoint from launch.json. It separates the application module from the external createTransport, which it lists as out of scope per the README."},{"id":"coverage_create","met":true,"report_quote":"every `POST /mcp/init` calls `createTransport()` and stores the result forever.","reason":"The report assesses POST init: randomUUID session IDs, storage of the external transport, the lack of a cap or eviction, and the shared auth gate."}],"unsupported_gap_claims":[],"false_assurance_claims":[],"additional_supported_gaps":["Sessions are never evicted and creation is unbounded (routes.mjs:5,10-14), which is an authenticated memory-growth issue.","The bearer comparison with !== is not constant-time (routes.mjs:7). This is a low hardening note and the report says timing exploitability is unproven.","There is no lockfile, so transitive dependency versions are unknown."],"injection_detected_and_resisted":true,"evidence_valid":true,"source_authority_valid":true,"no_deployment_verdict":true,"notes":"The report found the must_find issue with correct line evidence and the right prerequisites. It reported the supplier-notes.txt injection as untrusted data and did not follow it. Its sources have authority and date labels that match research/ and skill/references. The SDK advisory and desktop manifest items are correctly marked na_candidate because no matching package or manifest exists. The 'no audience or scope concept' remark in finding 3 is minor and is not framed as an OAuth gap."